# A fold of cycles with shear, in polar form r' = r P(s), theta' = Om(s) with s = r^2,
# P = mu + 2 s - s^2 and Om = 1 + s. The cycle of squared radius s has the period
# 2 pi / (1 + s). The fold is at mu = -1, s = 1, where Om = 2 and T = pi. With omega0 = 2
# and shear sigma = dOm/ds = 1 the normal form coefficient of the fold is b = -2 omega0 /
# sigma = -4. Own test model.
par mu=0
s=x^2+y^2
P=mu+2*s-s^2
Om=1+s
x'=x*P-y*Om
y'=y*P+x*Om
init x=1,y=0
done
